  "worked_solution": "Since the line $x=2$ is a vertical line, a perpendicular line would need to be horizontal. So, the perpendicular line must take the form $y=k$ for some value of $k.$\n\nThe perpendicular line needs to go through the point $(1,4),$ which has a $y$-coordinate of $4.$ So, the perpendicular line is $y=4.$",
